# Allowlist for agent-CLI invocations inside synced shell scripts.
# See .claude/lint-claude-cli-invocations.py — the lint hashes each
# `# claude-cli-invocations:start` / `:end` region and refuses to pass
# if the (hash, path) pair isn't listed here. Adding or rotating an
# entry requires byte-level review of the locked region in the same PR.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated): <sha256>  <path>  <description>
#
# The path field binds each approval to a specific source file —
# copying an allowlisted region into a new synced .sh file does NOT
# inherit the approval; the reviewer has to add a separate entry. Two
# roots holding byte-identical regions therefore need one entry each;
# that repetition is the binding working, not redundancy to collapse.
#
# Every description starts with one of two labels, so a reviewer can
# triage the list without opening every file:
#
#   LAUNCH:        a real unattended agent-CLI launch. Read the region.
#   NOT-A-LAUNCH:  a line the token scan matches but which starts no
#                  process — `claude` / `codex` / `gemini` appearing as a
#                  positional engine-id argument to a shell function.
#                  Locked anyway: the region hash is what makes an edit
#                  that turns one of these INTO a launch reviewer-visible.
#                  A rotation on one of these is normally a rename or an
#                  argument change, and should read as one in the diff.

6a803458acd032b7304b57d4a2d3934dd767905fb951cbb60ed970fe6f3e8abd  .claude/skills/agent-loop/scripts/agent-loop.sh  LAUNCH: agent-loop.sh default-worker Claude CLI command builder (--print --permission-mode bypassPermissions, optional --model)
c1246fd2f9865282be461bc38fba037662703a664bc6a864c840dd6b10d21f74  .claude/skills/critique/scripts/run-agy-review.sh  LAUNCH: bounded Agy reviewer; --model and --effort now come from review-profile.py launch-args (validated per engine) resolved inside this region; mode, permission, surface, output and timeout flags unchanged.

# --- Gemini harness root (.agents) ------------------------------------------
c2b9945797dafa63ac2f5fbe5836764c0c087acdebb1cb989f764aa94c60b170  .agents/skills/agent-loop/scripts/run-agy-launch.sh  LAUNCH: the shared exec point. `"$agy_cli" "$@"` with $agy_cli from ${AGY_CLI:-agy}. Both Gemini launchers route through here, so this one line decides which binary actually runs and with which argv; the token scan cannot see it (the binary name is variable-aliased), which is exactly why it is fenced by hand
cab649135162e117d4813b75921ad13e9bbb8c0ee9ae73a7fa99cd44ce61ec59  .agents/skills/agent-loop/scripts/run-agy-review.sh  LAUNCH: agent-loop Agy reviewer launch (--model from the --engine map, --effort, --mode accept-edits, --dangerously-skip-permissions, --disable-slash-commands, --add-dir <trusted root>, --output-format json, --print-timeout LOCAL_REVIEW_PASS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)
35b5fabecc5be530d2ac7d823201734024d7a1e0046e7b4399280c27043720d7  .agents/skills/agent-loop/scripts/run-agy-worker.sh  LAUNCH: agent-loop default Agy worker (--model from argv, --effort high, --mode accept-edits, --dangerously-skip-permissions, --disable-slash-commands, --output-format json, --print-timeout 60m). Unlike the reviewer this one has no --add-dir pin and a fixed 60m ceiling
a691801e45420a24b0ad278926f8dd8555f3cce901d33b1eda9a870bcfa45407  .agents/skills/agent-loop/scripts/agent-loop.sh  NOT-A-LAUNCH: `verify_v3_result_attestation Claude claude "$FILE" "$SIG"` — engine label and engine id passed to a shell function that verifies a stored attestation
7256706c226613b263d3cdc3ef0b03ea21113425358ef05f3010ab08bef17586  .agents/skills/agent-loop/scripts/agent-loop.sh  NOT-A-LAUNCH: `recover_v3_review_pass Claude claude "$round" "$round_base_sha"` — recovers an already-completed review leg from state; starts nothing
786965d5a8f1fcba3f16c43a612ce1462952f23edf0c5efe72dacb53aad24f64  .agents/skills/agent-loop/scripts/agent-loop.sh  NOT-A-LAUNCH: `run_review_pass Claude claude "$CLAUDE_REVIEW_HOOK" ...` — dispatches through the configured review hook; the hook itself is the launch surface and is fenced where it is built

# --- Codex harness root (.codex) --------------------------------------------
